From 0f5ff43afee27e0c2151b1d529d17c9395fa8873 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 18:22:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add PostGIS SQL report download, surface debris dimensions
 end-to-end

- New GET /logs/{log_id}/report.sql, backed by src/geolocation/postgis_export.py,
  which dumps a standalone .sql file against the real detections table (not the
  toy marine_debris table from the original standalone script) -- loadable via
  `psql -f report.sql` without a live Postgres connection.
- GET /logs/{log_id}/detections now attaches length_m/width_m/height_m/
  dimensions_estimated per row (via class_taxonomy.bbox_dimensions_m), closing
  the gap where the live dashboard had no dimension data to show at all.
- report.json/report.csv also gained length_m/width_m/height_m columns.
- Frontend: api.ts/data.ts carry the new fields through, Dashboard.tsx's
  DetailDialog (the actual live detection popup) now shows Length/Width/Height,
  and ReportsView gained a SQL download button next to CSV/JSON/GeoJSON/PDF.
- Guarded the two geometry test files' src.backend.main import so a missing
  torch/cv2 only skips their API-level test classes instead of failing
  collection for the whole file.

33 passed, 2 warnings (backend/tests). Frontend type-checks clean (tsc --noEmit).

